OpenSSL 4.1.0: no padding of the inner ALPN extension under ECH

Kuicksilver's own code, the ninth patch carried under ADR-0019 (docs/adr/0019-openssl-4-and-ech.md), applied after
openssl-4.1.0-ech-reject-client-flight.patch; pinned by its SHA-256 in gradle/openssl.toml as patch_9, applied by
tools/openssl/apply-patch.pl to the verified tarball, and dropped with the first OpenSSL release that offers it (an
upstream proposal is drafted, 2026-11-20, under openssl/openssl#33844).

The gap: RFC 9849 section 6.1.3 has a client pad the inner ClientHello for what varies between its connections:
"Clients SHOULD pad this extension [ALPN] by rounding up to the total size of the longest ALPN extension across all
application profiles." OpenSSL 4.1.0 pads only the server_name (ossl_ech_calc_padding) and has no API to pad anything
else, so two application profiles of one client (h3; h2 and http/1.1) give EncodedClientHelloInner lengths 9 octets
apart, visible in the payload length whenever that crosses a 32-octet step.

The change: SSL_CTX_ech_set_alpn_pad_target and SSL_ech_set_alpn_pad_target set the size, with its 4-octet header, of
the longest ALPN extension across the client's profiles (0, the default, pads none; above OSSL_ECH_MAX_ALPN_EXT_LEN
refused); ossl_ech_alpn_padding is max(0, target - the inner ALPN extension's size), which ossl_ech_calc_padding adds to
the server_name padding before the 32-octet rounding, and which a GREASE payload (the seventh patch's
ech_grease_clear_len) counts as a real offer would. New public functions: static builds only here, no libssl.num entry.

diff --git a/include/openssl/ech.h b/include/openssl/ech.h
--- a/include/openssl/ech.h
+++ b/include/openssl/ech.h
@@ -35,6 +35,8 @@
 #define OSSL_ECH_MAX_MAXNAMELEN 255 /* ECHConfig max for max name length */
 #define OSSL_ECH_MAX_PUBLICNAME 255 /* max ECHConfig public name length */
 #define OSSL_ECH_MAX_ALPNLEN 255 /* max alpn length */
+/* the largest ALPN extension: its type and length, then a protocol list of up to 2^16 - 1 octets */
+#define OSSL_ECH_MAX_ALPN_EXT_LEN (4 + 2 + 0xffff)
 #define OSSL_ECH_OUTERS_MAX 20 /* max extensions we compress via outer-exts */
 #define OSSL_ECH_ALLEXTS_MAX 32 /* max total number of extension we allow */
 
@@ -109,6 +111,13 @@
 int SSL_ech_set1_outer_alpn_protos(SSL *s, const unsigned char *protos,
     const size_t protos_len);
 
+/*
+ * RFC 9849, section 6.1.3: pad the inner ALPN extension up to target octets
+ * (with its 4-octet header): the size of the longest ALPN extension across
+ * the client's application profiles; 0 (the default) pads none. Returns 1 for
+ * success, 0 for a target above OSSL_ECH_MAX_ALPN_EXT_LEN.
+ */
+int SSL_ech_set_alpn_pad_target(SSL *s, size_t target);
 int SSL_ech_get1_status(SSL *s, char **inner_sni, char **outer_sni);
 int SSL_ech_set1_grease_suite(SSL *s, const char *suite);
